@@ -159,6 +159,19 @@ When you start Campfire for the first time, you'll be guided through creating an
 Campfire is single-tenant: any rooms designated "public" will be accessible by all users in the system.
 To support entirely distinct groups of customers, you would deploy multiple instances of the application.
 
+### Posting as a bot
+
+From **Account settings → Set up chat bots**, add a bot and copy its code. Bots join open rooms automatically; for a closed room, grant the bot access in the room settings. Use the room ID from the room’s URL and store the bot code in your CI secret store (`BOT_CODE` below).
+
+```sh
+curl --fail --data-binary 'Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅' \
+  "https://chat.example.com/rooms/${ROOM_ID}/${BOT_CODE}/messages"
+```
+
+Send plain UTF-8 text, not JSON or form fields. For an attachment instead, use `-F 'attachment=@build.log'`. A successful post returns `201` and the new message’s path in `Location`. A blank post returns `422`, an invalid code `401`, and a missing or inaccessible room `404`.
+
+Treat the entire webhook URL as a password. Use HTTPS, mask it in CI output, and redact this route in any proxy access logs or monitoring tools. The Docker image disables Thruster’s unredacted access log by default. Deleting the bot revokes its code without deleting its message history.
+
 ### Upgrading
 
 All of Campfire's state lives in the mounted volume, so upgrading is a matter of pulling a newer image and recreating the container:
diff --git a/lib/bot_message_request.rb b/lib/bot_message_request.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6ffae99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/bot_message_request.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Take the bearer credential out of the URL before Rails logs or instruments the
+# request. Upstream HTTP access logs must redact this route separately.
+class BotMessageRequest
+  PATH = %r{\A(/rooms/[^/]+/)([^/]+)(/messages/?)\z}
+
+  def initialize(app)
+    @app = app
+  end
+
+  def call(env)
+    if match = PATH.match(env["PATH_INFO"])
+      env["campfire.bot_code"] = match[2]
+      redacted_path = "#{match[1]}REDACTED#{match[3]}"
+      %w[ PATH_INFO REQUEST_PATH REQUEST_URI ORIGINAL_FULLPATH ].each do |key|
+        env[key] = env[key].sub(match[0]) { redacted_path } if env[key]
+      end
+
+      # curl -d defaults to form encoding. Don't let Rack interpret message
+      # text as parameters (including _method) or try to parse it as JSON.
+      env["CONTENT_TYPE"] = "text/plain" unless Rack::Request.new(env).media_type == "multipart/form-data"
+    end
+
+    @app.call(env)
+  end
+end
